From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Subject: MAINTAINERS: classify maple tree and XArray as MM components
Date: Sun, 01 Nov 2026 18:30:41 -0800

Rename MAPLE TREE to MEMORY MANAGEMENT - MAPLE TREE and XARRAY to MEMORY
MANAGEMENT - XARRAY.  Move both entries to their alphabetical positions
among the MM components.

These files were originally used only by MM, they remain primarily used by
MM and their maintainers are recognized members of the MM team.

Preserve every existing contact, status and file pattern in both entries.
Also add include/linux/radix-tree.h, lib/radix-tree.c, lib/radix-tree.h and
lib/test_ida.c to MEMORY MANAGEMENT - XARRAY.  Radix trees share node
infrastructure with XArray and IDR; IDA is implemented in the already-
covered lib/idr.c.

Add the following file assignments:

MEMORY MANAGEMENT - XARRAY
        include/linux/radix-tree.h
        lib/radix-tree.c
        lib/radix-tree.h
        lib/test_ida.c

The following existing patterns move unchanged with each entry:

MEMORY MANAGEMENT - MAPLE TREE
        Documentation/core-api/maple_tree.rst
        include/linux/maple_tree.h
        include/trace/events/maple_tree.h
        lib/maple_tree.c
        lib/region_alloc_benchmark.c
        lib/test_maple_tree.c
        rust/helpers/maple_tree.c
        rust/kernel/maple_tree.rs
        tools/testing/radix-tree/maple.c
        tools/testing/shared/linux/maple_tree.h

MEMORY MANAGEMENT - XARRAY
        Documentation/core-api/idr.rst
        Documentation/core-api/xarray.rst
        include/linux/idr.h
        include/linux/xarray.h
        lib/idr.c
        lib/region_alloc_benchmark.c
        lib/test_xarray.c
        lib/xarray.c
        tools/testing/radix-tree

Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: Liam R. Howlett <liam@infradead.org>
Cc: Alice Ryhl <aliceryhl@google.com>
Cc: Andrew Ballance <andrewjballance@gmail.com>
